  "current_warning": {
    "signal": "max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(max(abs(i(Vsense0_${id})),abs(i(Vsense1_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense2_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense3_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense4_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense5_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense6_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense7_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense8_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense9_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense10_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense11_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense12_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense13_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense14_${id}))),abs(i(Vsense15_${id})))",
    "limit_parameter": "warning_current"
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/cd74hc4067.pdf"
  ],
  "category": "Analog/Switches and multiplexers",
  "family": "74HC/HCT",
  "model_notes": [
    "Own compact model; manufacturer datasheets provide pinout, truth table and nominal electrical reference points.",
    "Analog paths are passive, bilateral conductances. They pass intermediate and negative voltages within the supply rails; they do not regenerate logic levels.",
    "On resistance interpolates the documented supply points and is flat with signal voltage. Below the first point it stays fixed; low-voltage accuracy is limited.",
    "Controls use logic-ground-referenced thresholds; floating or intermediate controls select no path. HCT thresholds are proportional values calibrated at 5 V.",
    "Separate turn-on/off event delays approximate control timing; turn_on > turn_off provides a nominal break-before-make interval for multiplexers. Delays do not vary with supply or load.",
    "Invalid or absent supply immediately opens all paths. No parasitic powering, clamp diodes, charge injection, exact crosstalk, thermal drift or damage is modeled.",
    "Keep analog ports within VEE/VSS and VCC. Off-state leakage is a fixed resistance; port and control capacitances are lumped estimates.",
    "Input-only ports do not drive their own nets; disconnected controls cannot select a path during startup. Requests circuit-wide Gear order 2 to damp abrupt contact changes, without a fixed small global timestep."
  ]
}
